kbi:R1 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R1 — Each stage has its own quality vocabulary; no umbrella QualityDimension across stages"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "RDODI procedure v1.2.0 stage-specific gates (Stage1–Stage4 each have their own acceptance gates); underlying vocabulary discipline is currently implicit." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R1_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R1" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R1_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R1_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-72 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R1 records that each RDODI stage has stage-specific quality vocabulary because a research-stage artifact's quality has nothing to do with keyboard-accessibility and an interactive-page-stage artifact's quality has nothing to do with Harvard citation form; a single umbrella QualityDimension class hides this fact."@en .

kbi:R10 a kb:CrossCuttingPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R10 — Disposition wording must be scoped to exactly what is being retired"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "A4_reference_template_disposition_v1_0_0.md correction section in predecessor v1.5.x." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R10_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R10" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R10_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R10_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-40 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R10 records that every RDODI disposition statement must name exactly what is being retired, what remains intact, and what becomes of the residual; the A4 disposition's first wording over-reached and was corrected."@en .

kbi:R11 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R11 — Tier-maximizing reference resolution: upgrade each citation to the highest reachable authority tier before accepting any lower rank; decrease-and-conquer for economy"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Test-driven in current session (2026-05-29) on Ch.9's 21-reference bibliography against catalogue v1.1.0 authority tiers. Single-pass authoritative-tier confirmations: PMBOK 2013 -> Definitive (LoC CIP, LCCN 2012046112); Deming 1982 -> High (WorldCat OCLC 13126265, correcting a prior wrong LCCN); Boehm 1981 -> High (ACM DL + WorldCat OCLC 7734154); Besterfield 1999 -> High (Taylor & Francis review record, ISBN 0-13-639403-5); plus earlier ACM/SEI confirmations Humphrey (DOI 10.1109/52.2014, issue-number corrected 3->2), Paulk (IEEE Software 10(6), issue corrected 4->6), Florac (SEI Definitive, CMU/SEI-97-HB-003). Each confirmed reference left the work set after one pass."@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R11_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R11" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R11_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R11_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R11 governs how RDODI resolves bibliographic references against the tiered BibliographicCatalogue (kbx authority tiers: Definitive>High>Moderate>Low). For each reference, the resolver MUST attempt the HIGHEST authority tier first and accept a lower tier ONLY after higher tiers are shown unreachable. Procedure per reference: (1) issue a LOOSE high-recall query to the delivering channel (web_search), deliberately broad rather than exact — the probabilistic pre-filter, analogous to a Bloom-filter membership pre-test; (2) PARSE the returned candidate set for membership of an authoritative-tier catalogue record (Definitive: LoC/SEI/ISO/etc.; High: Crossref-DOI/WorldCat-OCLC/ACM/IEEE/DBLP/T&F) matching the reference on author+title+year(+identifier); (3) the parse-match against the record's OWN stated metadata is the authoritative confirmation step — a candidate merely appearing in the set is the pre-filter signal, never the verdict (a Low-tier sales listing in the set does NOT promote the tier); (4) the MOMENT an authoritative-tier match is confirmed, STOP and remove the reference from the work set — do not search it again (decrease-and-conquer); (5) only if no authoritative member appears after loose passes does the resolver descend to the next tier, recording the honest highest tier actually reached; (6) where no catalogue of any tier contains the work (e.g. ephemeral trade-press web articles), record Unresolvable with reason — the Bloom 'definitely not present' verdict — rather than borrowing a higher label. ECONOMY: because confirmed references leave the work set permanently, total queries are bounded by the count of as-yet-unconfirmed references, not by tier-count x reference-count; high-value references typically resolve in ONE pass. CORRECTNESS: tier-first prevents settling for a commercial-listing 'CatalogueVerified' when an authoritative record was reachable, and the breadth of the loose pull surfaces edition/identifier disambiguations that exact single-shot queries miss."@en .

kbi:R12 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R12 — The interactive-page (Stage-4) stage is gated GENERATION, not deterministic rendering: an LLM shapes the page from the grounded graph (creativity is the asset), and fidelity gates defend grounding; the two co-evolve by iteration until BOTH a mechanical stop (the gate stops catching real infidelity) and a human stop (the result satisfies the bar) are met"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "DECIDED direction (this session, user-confirmed). Status Proposed — NOT AlreadyAdopted — because the page-stage application has not yet been demonstrated producing a bar-grade page; per L-65 the next action is the first loop iteration as the test drive that confirms or corrects R12. The gated-co-evolution METHOD itself is session-demonstrated (the recurring build->test->catch->fix loop across F53/F57/F58/F71 and the two-broken-then-fixed renderer this session); the F50 fidelity harness it depends on is DESIGNED but NOT BUILT."@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R12_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R12" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R12_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:Proposed ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R12_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R12 records the decided architecture for the Stage-4 interactive page. A test drive (this session) proved a PURE deterministic renderer can emit grounded HTML from the page-ABox with full traceability (1981 blocks, 0 untraced) BUT the output is mechanical documentation — unshaped, ~2x the deployed bar in size yet below it in curation (1 table vs 7-12; 1116 flat citation chips vs 70-154 woven). The shaping a deployed-bar page needs — which of N claims to weave inline, prose vs table vs quiz, sequencing, framing — is an irreducibly GENERATIVE/editorial act a pure function cannot perform. Therefore the page stage is correctly an LLM-shapes-under-gates step: the LLM gets latitude over FORM (ordering, emphasis, surfacing, pedagogical framing) but NEVER over FACTS (no invented claim, no altered identifier, no changed metric, no relation absent from the graph). Every shaped element must trace to a source triple, checked AFTER generation by a fidelity harness (the F50/F46 design: FaithfulnessError, GroundingScore, ReferenceIntegrity, CountDrift) — the gates become fidelity checks against the source graph, not element counters. The chicken-and-egg (cannot fully specify the gate before seeing what the generator drifts on; cannot tune the generator before the gate locates the drift) is resolved by ITERATION, not by sequencing: harness and generator co-evolve, each iteration sharpening both. SAFETY RAIL (reframed from F50's 'no prose ships until harness built'): the harness must exist and RUN each iteration before that iteration's output is TRUSTED or shipped — generating prose to FEED the gate is the engine of the loop; believing prose WITHOUT the gate is the failure mode. The difference is candidate (fine) vs result (not until gated). STOP CONDITIONS (both required): mechanical (harness goes quiet on genuine infidelity) AND human (the read satisfies the bar) — a clean harness on a lifeless page is not done; a beautiful ungated page is not done. RESIDUE (honest, per F53): predicate-faithfulness among co-occurring concepts is the part a mechanical check can only ROUTE to human/LLM-judge review, never auto-confirm — that residue is the permanent human-verifier role (the §1 constraint), not a defect to engineer away."@en .

kbi:R13 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R13 — Record lessons as they emerge: a release is not complete until new lessons surfaced this session are written to the governed store"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Practiced this session (findings F71–F107 each recorded as they emerged); formalized as a gate 2026-06-04 on assessment of OE proposal item R."@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R13_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R13" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R13_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R13_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-64 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R13 governs lesson capture across an RDODI session. Lessons learned MUST be recorded into the governed knowledge store AS THEY EMERGE within a session, not merely cited or deferred to session end. A session that applies and cites discipline but adds NO new lessons despite clear new ones having surfaced is itself a governance gap. Enforcement is a release-completeness gate: before any release is considered complete, the session must answer 'were new lessons that emerged this session recorded?' — a negative answer blocks the release-complete claim (not the artifact's correctness, which other gates check). The gate targets the capture process, not within-artifact validity. Originated as a cross-session OE proposal (a parallel session, 2026-06-03, proposal item R); assessed and adopted into RDODI under its own discipline because the lesson is about the governance PROCESS that RDODI runs each session. Distinct from L-65 (verify before publishing) which governs claim truth, and from the stage-conformance gate which governs artifact typing — R13 governs whether emergent knowledge was captured at all."@en .

kbi:R14 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R14 — Conformance is necessary but not sufficient for quality: a stage gate guarantees a correct artifact, not a good one; gate the floor, keep the human on the ceiling"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Discovered this session (2026-06-04): interactive page v2.0.0 PASSED the stage-conformance gate yet was judged inadequate; quality arrived only via human-driven redesign rounds v3.0.0/v4.0.0 (findings F100, F102, F105)."@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R14_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R14" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R14_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:Proposed ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R14_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R14 records that passing a stage-conformance gate (artifact typed against its ontology, SHACL-valid, faithful to source) does NOT guarantee design/pedagogical quality. The two are different axes: conformance governs correctness; design quality governs richness, density balance, usability and aptness. A future RDODI page can be CONFORMANT yet thin or poorly designed. Therefore the standard is reproducible at the FLOOR (faithful + typed + SHACL-valid, fully gated) but not at the CEILING (taste, apt visualization, genuine pedagogical value, which remain human judgment). Operational consequence: do not treat a green conformance verdict as a quality verdict; raise a separate design-quality FLOOR (e.g. >=1 non-text encoding per major section, declared usability heuristics, real-browser zero-console-error) so no artifact ships thin or unchecked, while routing the un-gatable ceiling to human review. Mirrors the F39/F53 warrant residue one level up: mechanism routes judgment, it cannot manufacture it."@en .

kbi:R15 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R15 — A cross-session claim is a hypothesis to verify on local disk, never a fact to import; a lead false in one session can be true in another"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Practiced twice this session (2026-06-04): the R11 web_search pre-filter proposal (F107) and the OE/RDODI lesson proposals (F108) were each re-verified on local disk before action."@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R15_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R15" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R15_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R15_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-64 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R15 governs how RDODI treats claims, proposals, or artifacts originating in a PARALLEL session. Every such claim — even one tagged 'verified' by its author — was verified against THAT session's disk, not this one, and MUST be independently re-verified against the receiving session's own files before any action. Membership of a claim in a proposal is only a pre-filter signal, never a verdict (compare R11's Bloom-filter discipline for references). Critically, a lead can be FALSE in its origin session and TRUE in the receiving one (or vice versa): a named artifact reported 'not found' elsewhere may exist here, and a path/version cited from another session may be stale locally. Therefore: re-run the check on local disk; correct cross-session leads in either direction; import no foreign code or state; label any adopted item by its LOCAL grounding (the receiving session's ABox/spec), not by the foreign claim. Composes with OE L-64 but is a DISTINCT axis: L-64 governs SCOPE (cross-session content is assessed, not edited); R15 governs VERIFICATION (cross-session claims are re-verified locally, not trusted)."@en .

kbi:R2 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R2 — Quality does not propagate across pipeline stages"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Stage4.H/I/J widget gates and Stage4.K intention-coverage in procedure v1.2.0 implement this lesson; the underlying principle is not yet named in any procedure note or blueprint finding." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R2_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R2" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R2_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R2_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R2 records that an upstream PASS never licenses a downstream PASS in the RDODI pipeline; a polished research report does not yield a polished interactive page automatically, which is why every stage has its own gates and the widget-stage adoption (Stage4.H–K) was necessary."@en .

kbi:R3 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R3 — Intention-coverage is ONE-HOP; schema settled by test-drive on a separating case"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "intention_coverage_gate_v1_0_0.py (Stage4.K) with adversarial test 7/7; rationale currently held as F65 in predecessor methodology blueprint." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R3_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R3" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R3_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R3_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-66 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R3 records that the coverage-unit in intention_coverage_gate is the intention (LearningObjective), not the subject the intention is about; the two-hop schema was rejected by building a separating case in which two intentions share one subject and the manifests differ on coverage status."@en .

kbi:R4 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R4 — Asymmetric coverage gate: widget-without-intention FAILS; intention-without-widget DISCLOSES"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Procedure v1.1.0 Stage4.K and intention_coverage_gate; pattern is already operational." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R4_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R4" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R4_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R4_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-40 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R4 records that coverage gates should not be symmetric by default: a page can never demonstrate everything in the ontology so uncovered intentions are honest scope-disclosure (reported, not failed) but interactivity that demonstrates nothing is decoration and fails."@en .

kbi:R5 a kb:RDODISpecificPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R5 — The negative-exemplar pattern: ship at least one worked example designed to FAIL the gates"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "Ch.9 worked example in predecessor session: 0/27 widget markers, fails Stage4.H/I/J/K by design. This current session's Ch.9 v1.5.0 bundle is positive-grade and does NOT yet ship a paired negative exemplar." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R5_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R5" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R5_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:Proposed ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R5_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R5 records that every gated RDODI pipeline must ship at least one negative worked example whose gates fail by design, with the failure mode stated; without a negative exemplar the gates have no demonstrable load-bearing evidence."@en .

kbi:R6 a kb:CrossCuttingPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R6 — '0 violations' / conformance claims must name shape version AND method"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "RDODI_OE_ASSESSMENT_BASELINE_v1_0_0.md correction section in v1.5.1; wording rule applies forward." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R6_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R6" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R6_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R6_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R6 records that any conformance claim in RDODI documentation must name shape version, imports policy, corpus scope, and exclusions in the same sentence; under-specified zero-violation claims were caught by parallel-OE review and corrected in v1.5.1."@en .

kbi:R7 a kb:CrossCuttingPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R7 — Two-rounds-of-guessing antipattern: stop on the second identical user challenge"@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R7_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R7" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R7_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:Proposed ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R7_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-40 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R7 records that when a user repeats the same challenge against an RDODI build or decision, the next action is a direct ask rather than another iteration; the line-1259 incident in the predecessor session is the canonical case."@en .

kbi:R8 a kb:CrossCuttingPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R8 — Cross-LLM bibliography labels: CORROBORATED, not VERIFIED"@en ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R8_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R8" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R8_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:Proposed ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R8_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:BP-D41 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R8 records that any reference list reaching RDODI's reference rule via a parallel LLM session must be labeled CORROBORATED until resolved against an authoritative non-LLM source; BP-D41 verification cannot be satisfied by another LLM's claim."@en .

kbi:R9 a kb:CrossCuttingPattern,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R9 — Adversarial harness tests must be hermetic from the package"@en ;
    kb:adoptionLocation "02-gates/rdodi_gate_adversarial_test_v1_2_0.py + 02-gates/fixtures/ in predecessor v1.5.1; pattern applies forward." ;
    kb:coversExisting kbi:R9_cov1 ;
    kb:patternCode "R9" ;
    kb:patternEvidence kbi:R9_ev1 ;
    kb:patternStatus kb:AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel ;
    kb:recommendsIntegration kbi:R9_int1 ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "Pattern R9 records that all RDODI adversarial tests must resolve paths via __file__ and bundle every fixture; the remediation from rdodi_gate_adversarial_test v1.1.0 (5 absolute paths, 3 unbundled fixtures) to v1.2.0 (hermetic, 13/13 reproducible from files) is the canonical implementation."@en .

