kbi:R10_int1 a kb:MethodologyNoteRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R10 integration: disposition wording rule"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "Every RDODI disposition statement names exactly what is being retired, what remains intact, and what becomes of the residual; over-reaching wording must be corrected with a visible correction section, not silently rewritten." .

kbi:R11_cov1 a kb:CoverageCheck,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R11 coverage: relation to existing OE discipline and the catalogue authority-tier layer"@en ;
    kb:coversExisting "OE L-65 (verify before publishing); kbx CatalogueAuthorityTier layer (KB-EXT v1.1.0); session confirmability principle"@en ;
    skos:definition "R11 does not duplicate existing discipline; it composes two existing pieces into a procedure. It depends on the kbx CatalogueAuthorityTier layer (KB-EXT v1.1.0) for the tier ranking it maximizes against, and it operationalizes OE L-65 (verify before publishing) and the session's confirmability principle (non-model oracle disposes). It is distinct from OE BP-D codes, which govern artifact naming/versioning/manifests, not citation-resolution tiering. No existing RDODI pattern R1-R10 covers reference-resolution tier strategy."@en .

kbi:R11_ev1 a kb:ArtifactReference,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R11 evidence: runtime resolution results recorded this session"@en ;
    kb:provenanceSession "2026-05-29 Ch.9 confirmability resolution session" ;
    skos:definition "Evidence is the runtime web_search/parse output captured in /home/claude/ch9_resolution/RESOLUTION_METHOD_NOTE_v1_0_0.md and the tiered worklist table, showing per-reference highest-tier-reached verdicts and the catalogue records that produced them. Status AlreadyAdoptedAtGateLevel (not merely Proposed) is justified per L-65 because the pattern was demonstrated working BEFORE being recorded: five references reached authoritative tier in single passes and two source errors were caught by the method."@en .

kbi:R11_int1 a kb:ProcedureAddendumRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R11 integration: procedure addendum + blueprint methodology note mandating tier-maximizing resolution"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "RDODI reference resolution MUST be tier-maximizing: for each reference, attempt the highest authority tier first (per the kbx CatalogueAuthorityTier ranking), using a loose high-recall query as a probabilistic pre-filter and an authoritative-record parse-match as the confirmation step; stop and retire the reference from the work set on first authoritative confirmation (decrease-and-conquer); descend to a lower tier only after higher tiers are shown unreachable; and record Unresolvable-with-reason rather than label a reference above the tier of the source that actually confirmed it."@en ;
    skos:definition "Recommended integration into the RDODI four-stage procedure (Stage 1 Research / reference handling) and the methodology blueprint: when resolving any external reference, apply R11 — highest tier first, loose-query-then-parse-for-authoritative-member, stop-on-confirm, descend only on demonstrated unreachability, record Unresolvable rather than borrow a higher label. The addendum makes tier-maximization the default resolution discipline, not an optional pass."@en .

kbi:R12_cov1 a kb:CoverageCheck,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R12 coverage: relation to F50/F46 harness design, F53 residue, the §1 constraint, and the discourse-selection stage"@en ;
    kb:coversExisting "F50/F46 fidelity-harness design (to be built); F53 escalation-tier; §1 generator-cannot-self-certify constraint; discourse-selection stage; F39 silent-rewording risk"@en ;
    skos:definition "R12 does not invent new machinery; it commits the page stage to the architecture the blueprint's own findings were converging on. It depends on the F50/F46 fidelity-harness DESIGN (FaithfulnessError/GroundingScore/ReferenceIntegrityGate/CountDrift) — which R12 requires be BUILT and adversarially proven (F39 showed a frontier LLM silently reworded 7/13 entities uncaught by naive checks). It inherits F53's escalation-tier for the predicate-faithfulness residue, and it is the page-stage instance of the §1 constraint (generator cannot self-certify; human is permanent verifier). It uses, not duplicates, RDODI's existing discourse-selection stage (which already CHOOSES per-section widgets). No existing pattern R1-R11 covers the render-vs-generation architecture decision for Stage-4."@en .

kbi:R12_ev1 a kb:ArtifactReference,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R12 evidence: the deterministic-render test drive that motivated the gated-generation decision"@en ;
    kb:provenanceSession "2026-05-29 Ch.9 page-stage architecture session" ;
    skos:definition "Evidence is the test-drive renderer render_page_testdrive_v0_1_0.py + its traceability ledger (1981 blocks, 0 untraced, valid HTML) and the bar-measurement showing the render is faithful-but-unshaped (264KB, 1 table, 1116 flat cites vs the deployed bar of 117-140KB, 7-12 tables, 70-154 woven cites). The render CONFIRMED the page can be graph-derived AND established that shaping is the missing, irreducibly generative capability — the empirical basis for choosing gated generation over deterministic rendering for this stage."@en .

kbi:R12_int1 a kb:ProcedureAddendumRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R12 integration: Stage-4 procedure becomes gated co-evolution; harness-runs-each-iteration safety rail"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "RDODI Stage-4 page generation is gated co-evolution: an LLM shapes the page from the grounded graph (latitude over form, never over facts), a fidelity harness checks every shaped element traces to a source triple (grounding, citation-identifier integrity, numeric fidelity, entity membership) each iteration, the predicate-faithfulness residue is escalated to human/LLM-judge review rather than auto-confirmed, and the loop iterates until both the harness goes quiet on genuine infidelity AND the result satisfies the deployed bar. No iteration output is shipped until it has passed the current harness."@en ;
    skos:definition "Recommended integration into the RDODI four-stage procedure §5 (interactive page): replace 'deterministic render' / 'count >=N elements' with the gated-co-evolution loop — LLM shapes from the graph; the fidelity harness runs each iteration; caught infidelities become generator constraints or new harness checks; the predicate residue escalates to review; iterate to the two-condition stop. The element-COUNT gates (Stage4.D) are superseded by fidelity gates per the count-not-substance lesson. PREREQUISITE (fail-stop, reframed): no iteration's output is trusted/shipped until that iteration has passed the current harness; the harness is built up THROUGH the loop, not fully before it."@en .

kbi:R13_cov1 a kb:PatternCoverage,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R13 coverage / non-duplication"@en ;
    skos:definition "R13 does not duplicate existing RDODI items: no session-close / release-completeness lessons-recorded gate exists in the RDODI knowledge base prior to this addition (verified by scanning all skos:definition text for record-as-emerge / session-close / lessons-recorded concepts — zero hits). It composes with L-65 (verify before publish) and the OE B1/L-64 cross-session boundary, and is enforced via a new pre-ship checklist item in the enforcement stage. The OE-targeted sibling proposals O/P/Q (per-project isolation, standard-interface, present-only-asked) are operational to their originating workstream and OE-targeted; they are NOT adopted into RDODI (cross-study hygiene) and are forwarded to the OE session unchanged."@en .

kbi:R13_ev1 a kb:PatternEvidence,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R13 evidence"@en ;
    skos:definition "The originating OE proposal's own evidence: an earlier parallel session applied and cited lessons for many turns but recorded none until an examiner challenge prompted it — the governance gap R13 names. Counter-evidence that the gate is followable: in the present RDODI session, findings F71 through F107 were each recorded into the methodology blueprint as they emerged, demonstrating the behavior the gate makes non-skippable."@en .

kbi:R13_int1 a kb:PatternIntegration,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R13 recommended integration"@en ;
    skos:definition "Integrate R13 as a release-completeness gate in the RDODI operating checklist (section D, before ship): 'D4 — new lessons recorded? If lessons emerged this session, they are written to the governed store before the release is called complete.' Blocking for the release-complete CLAIM, not for artifact correctness. Wired into rdodi_alert_manifest as a blocking pre-ship check."@en .

kbi:R14_cov1 a kb:PatternCoverage,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R14 cov1"@en ;
    skos:definition "R14 does not duplicate existing RDODI patterns: R1 (stage-specific quality vocabulary) and R12 (page architecture) concern WHICH gate/structure applies, not the conformance-vs-design-quality distinction; R2 (upstream pass != downstream pass) is about cross-stage licensing, a different axis. No prior pattern states conformance != design quality."@en .

kbi:R14_ev1 a kb:PatternEvidence,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R14 ev1"@en ;
    skos:definition "Evidence: v2.0.0 was CONFORMANT (typed ABox, SHACL-valid, faithful) and still 'behind the standards' per the user; the design-quality finding F105 documented that the interactive-page ontology already carries unused QualityDimension/QualityAssessment/UsabilityHeuristic vocabulary, and that no design-quality floor gate existed."@en .

kbi:R14_int1 a kb:PatternIntegration,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R14 int1"@en ;
    skos:definition "Integrate R14 as a standing caution wherever a conformance gate is run, and as the rationale for a Stage-4 design-quality FLOOR gate (proposed, not yet built) reusing the ontology's QualityDimension/UsabilityHeuristic vocabulary. The gate enforces a richness floor; human review owns the ceiling."@en .

kbi:R15_cov1 a kb:PatternCoverage,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R15 cov1"@en ;
    skos:definition "R15 does not duplicate OE L-64 (scope: assessed-not-edited) — it adds the VERIFICATION axis (re-verify-locally). It also does not duplicate R13 (whose cross-session mention is mere provenance of its origin, not a rule about treating cross-session claims)."@en .

kbi:R15_ev1 a kb:PatternEvidence,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R15 ev1"@en ;
    skos:definition "Evidence: in F107 the proposal's [VERIFIED-HERE] tags were re-checked here and a cross-session lead was CORRECTED in our favor (RESOLUTION_METHOD_NOTE_v1_0_0.md was reported 'not found' on the proposing session's disk but EXISTS here at ch9_resolution/); in F108 the proposal's lesson-count and anchor BPs were re-verified against this session's OE ABox (SHA eeb61ab19...) and a self-corrected count error (LessonsLearned type localname) was caught rather than asserted."@en .

kbi:R15_int1 a kb:PatternIntegration,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R15 int1"@en ;
    skos:definition "Integrate R15 as the standing rule whenever a parallel-session proposal/artifact is received: re-verify every claim on local disk first; correct leads in either direction; import no foreign code/state; ground adopted items locally. Wire as a checklist precondition for any cross-session-originated task."@en .

kbi:R1_cov1 a kb:CoverageCheck,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R1 coverage: BP-D32 adjacent but not equivalent"@en ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:BP-D32 ;
    skos:definition "BP-D32 (InteractivityCouplingMustEncodeDomainSemantics) addresses interactivity-domain coupling, not quality-vocabulary-by-stage; the gates implement R1 implicitly but no BP/L explicitly states the vocabulary-by-stage principle."@en .

kbi:R1_ev1 a kb:TranscriptCitation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R1 evidence: transcript line 6534"@en ;
    kb:provenanceSession "predecessor-session (not locally re-verifiable in this current RDODI session)" ;
    kb:quotedSourceText "Each stage's quality is shaped by what that stage produces. A research artefact's quality has nothing to do with whether buttons are keyboard-accessible; an interactive page's quality has nothing to do with Harvard citation form. Collapsing them into one QualityDimension class with 8 named instances (the way the legacy bundle did) hides this fact." ;
    kb:transcriptLineRef 6534 ;
    skos:definition "Transcript citation at line 6534 of the predecessor RDODI session establishing the stage-specific quality vocabulary pattern."@en .

kbi:R1_int1 a kb:MethodologyNoteRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R1 integration: methodology note on stage-specific quality vocabulary"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "The RDODI quality vocabulary uses stage-specific subclasses (already followed in stage-specific gates). SHACL shapes attach to the stage-specific classes, narrower not broader. When future quality vocabulary is added, do not introduce an umbrella class spanning stages." ;
    skos:definition "The recommended integration is a methodology note recording that the RDODI quality vocabulary uses stage-specific subclasses; SHACL shapes attach to the stage-specific classes, narrower not broader; future quality vocabulary additions must not introduce an umbrella class spanning stages."@en .

kbi:R2_cov1 a kb:CoverageCheck,
