kbi:R3_int1 a kb:BlueprintFindingRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R3 integration: method-pattern finding F72 (proposed)"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "When a schema choice has a separating case (an input on which the readings yield different output), the test-drive — not preference — is what decides. The richer-looking option may lose on evidence (two-hop did)." ;
    skos:definition "Recommended integration: a methodology-blueprint method-pattern finding (proposed F72) stating that schema forks with separating cases are decided by test-drive rather than preference."@en .

kbi:R4_cov1 a kb:CoverageCheck,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R4 coverage: L-40 addresses disclosure language not asymmetric design"@en ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-40 ;
    skos:definition "L-40 addresses disclosure language for observations vs decisions but does not address the asymmetric pass/fail design principle itself; R4 adds the design-pattern dimension."@en .

kbi:R4_ev1 a kb:ArtifactReference,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R4 evidence: F66 in methodology_blueprint, intention_coverage_gate source"@en ;
    kb:externalReference "F66 in methodology_blueprint_v1_29_0; gate file present in current ecosystem at 06-widget-stage/02-gates/intention_coverage_gate_v1_0_0.py" ;
    kb:provenanceSession "predecessor-session" ;
    kb:quotedSourceText "a widget covering no declared intention = FAIL (decoration). An intention with no widget = DISCLOSED SCOPE (reported, NOT a fail)." ;
    skos:definition "Evidence is the predecessor blueprint finding F66 and the verbatim comment in the gate source code stating the asymmetric pass/fail design."@en .

kbi:R4_int1 a kb:BlueprintFindingRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R4 integration: design-pattern finding F73 (proposed)"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "When designing any coverage gate in the RDODI procedure (or extending it), explicitly answer two questions: (a) which direction is a real defect (the thing the gate must fail on), (b) which direction is honest scope-disclosure (the thing the gate must report-but-not-fail). Default-symmetric coverage gates either over-strict or over-permissive; the asymmetry must be intentional." ;
    skos:definition "Recommended integration: blueprint design-pattern finding (proposed F73) requiring every coverage gate to answer two questions — which direction is a real defect and which direction is honest scope-disclosure — and to make the asymmetry intentional rather than default-symmetric."@en .

kbi:R5_cov1 a kb:CoverageCheck,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R5 coverage: L-65 verifies gates fail on bad input but does not require shipping the bad input"@en ;
    kb:relatedOEDiscipline oe:L-65 ;
    skos:definition "L-65 requires that gates fail on bad input as part of verify-before-publishing; R5 adds the design counterpart — ship a permanent worked example that triggers the failure, so the gate's load-bearing nature is permanently demonstrable."@en .

kbi:R5_ev1 a kb:SessionDecisionRecord,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R5 evidence: CLEAN_SESSION_BOOTSTRAP_v1_2_0 closure record"@en ;
    kb:provenanceSession "predecessor-session (current ecosystem ships CLEAN_SESSION_BOOTSTRAP_v1_2_1 in 05-documentation/)" ;
    kb:quotedSourceText "The worked example is a NEGATIVE exemplar by design — has 0 of everything the gates check." ;
    skos:definition "Evidence is the closure record in the predecessor session's CLEAN_SESSION_BOOTSTRAP_v1_2_0 documenting Ch.9 as the negative exemplar."@en .

kbi:R5_int1 a kb:ProcedureAddendumRecommendation,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "R5 integration: procedure addendum mandating a negative exemplar"@en ;
    kb:proposedAddendumText "The RDODI procedure requires that every gated pipeline ship at least one negative worked example — an artifact the gates fail on by design, with the failure mode stated. A pipeline that only ships positive examples cannot be trusted to gate anything. The EX gap (no positive exemplar yet) is the other side of this discipline; both are required, neither substitutes for the other." ;
    skos:definition "Recommended integration: a procedure addendum requiring every gated RDODI pipeline to ship at least one negative worked example with its failure mode stated."@en .

